ds [rhetoric, logic and grammar] were not matters for gentlemen but schoolmasters, frequently Greeks, slaves or freedmen." <br>Brennan (2004) refers to "specialists in jurisprudence" during Republican Rome. "Certainly by c. 200 B.C. the Roman elite was taking an academic interest in the city-state\'s legal history." "In the developed Republic ... some important colleges of priests maintained books of precedents; the senate\'s part decrees could be consulted in written form." Latin legal literature began to develop c.200 BCE.<br>'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 2826, 'temperature': 0.2})
